    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Long before settlers, the Nanticoke and Nause-Waiwash peoples fished, crabbied, and foraged along the Nanticoke River and Fishing Bay near Elliott.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_maryland",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Elliott’s residents have traditionally depended on oystering, crabbing, and fishing, a livelihood shaped by the island’s marshy wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_maryland",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s centerpiece, the Elliott United Methodist Church, rose in stages from 1891 to 1905 after earlier fires, and its adjacent cemetery dates back to the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elliott sits on an island near the Blackwater National Wildlife Refuge, blending a tight‑knit community with a vital migratory bird habitat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elliott%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Access to Elliott is limited to a single 18‑mile blacktop path, Elliott Island Scenic Road, winding through marshes to U.S. Route 50 at Vienna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/elliott_maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "With an average elevation of just 3 feet above sea level, Elliott’s low‑lying marshes make it vulnerable to sea‑level rise and storm surges.",
